{"query":"Search for sworn congressional testimony or DOJ/FBI statements specifically describing when and how the FBI obtained the laptop and its chain of custody.","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"vault.fbi.gov","snippet":"The Vault is our new FOIA Library, containing 6,700 documents and other media that have been scanned from paper into digital copies so you can read them in the comfort of your home or office.","title":"FBI — Federal Bureau of Investigation","url":"https://vault.fbi.gov/search"},{"position":2,"site_name":"vault.fbi.gov","snippet":"The FBI's mission demands organizational accountability. Public trust must be earned, and transparency is not optional—it is essential. To that end, the FBI Vault features a collection of documents and other media that have been processed under the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA). These files have been released either as proactive disclosures or as frequently requested FBI records.","title":"FBI — Federal Bureau of Investigation","url":"https://vault.fbi.gov/"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.grassley.senate.gov","snippet":"Since 2020, we have conducted oversight of the Federal Bureau of Investigation's (FBI) corrupt handling of Hunter Biden's laptop. While your predecessor opted to stonewall and ignore our multiple requests for information on the matter, we expect that under your leadership the FBI will be transparent with Congress. The American people deserve to see every document, along with a detailed ...","title":"Johnson, Grassley to FBI - Hunter Biden Laptop, FBI Messages","url":"https://www.grassley.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/johnson_grassley_to_fbi_-_hunter_biden_laptop_fbi_messages.pdf"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.fbi.gov","snippet":"The Vault is the FBI's electronic FOIA Library, containing nearly 7,000 documents and other media that have been scanned from paper into digital copies so you can read them in the comfort of your ...","title":"FBI Vault — FBI","url":"https://www.fbi.gov/how-we-can-help-you/more-fbi-services-and-information/freedom-of-information-privacy-act/vault"},{"date":"Jul 20, 2023","position":5,"site_name":"judiciary.house.gov","snippet":"Put simply, after the FBI conditioned social media companies to believe that the laptop was the product of a hack-and-dump operation, the Bureau stopped its information sharing, allowing social media companies to conclude that the New York Post story was Russian disinformation. The Post published its story early in the morning on October 14.","title":"Testimony Reveals FBI Employees Who Warned Social Media ...","url":"https://judiciary.house.gov/media/press-releases/testimony-reveals-fbi-employees-who-warned-social-media-companies-about-hack"},{"date":"Apr 10, 2025","position":6,"site_name":"www.judiciary.senate.gov","snippet":"The American people deserve to see every document, along with a detailed explanation of how the FBI handled the laptop since the day they first possessed it on December 9, 2019,” the chairmen continued. Grassley and Johnson requested the following information:","title":"Grassley, Johnson Seek Explanation from FBI on Handling of ...","url":"https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/press/rep/releases/grassley-johnson-seek-explanation-from-fbi-on-handling-of-hunter-bidens-laptop"},{"date":"Jul 20, 2023","position":7,"site_name":"judiciary.house.gov","snippet":"On July 17, 2023, the Committee conducted a transcribed interview of Laura Dehmlow, the Section Chief of the FBI's Foreign Influence Task Force (FITF). During her transcribed interview, Dehmlow revealed that the same FBI personnel who were warning social media companies about a potential Russian 'hack and leak' operation in the run-up to the 2020 election knew that the laptop belonging to ...","title":"The Post - House Judiciary Committee Republicans","url":"https://judiciary.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/republicans-judiciary.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/2023-07-20-jdj-to-wray-re-dehmlow-testimony.pdf"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}